#prop:cubic-classification","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":4,"section_title":"The cubic alternative","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:3184ea73bfe67f7ff8187caf9c3ff220064aff724d8929e4f84d76c18f5f8fb2","file":"preprints/Exact-Fourier-certificates-for-complex-Hadamard-matrices-of-order-six-September-24-2026/build/sections/03-cubic.tex","line":12,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"61c04f19393f82eb14592408baf665a5ad25b5482377f6437f43098aac46f826","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Exact-Fourier-certificates-for-complex-Hadamard-matrices-of-order-six-September-24-2026/build/sections/03-cubic.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:3184ea73bfe67f7ff8187caf9c3ff220064aff724d8929e4f84d76c18f5f8fb2","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Exact-Fourier-certificates-for-complex-Hadamard-matrices-of-order-six-September-24-2026/build/sections/03-cubic.tex#L12"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{prop:cubic-classification}\nSuppose that $H$ and its entrywise square $H^{\\circ2}$ are Hadamard\nmatrices of order six. By multiplying rows and columns by unit complex\nnumbers and permuting rows and columns, one can transform $H$ into the\nmatrix $T$ in \\eqref{eq:cubic-matrix}.\nIn particular, every entry of the transformed matrix is a cube root of\nunity."}
